(5452172, 784049, 86447, '<td valign="top">Gee.   Good grammar should not be relinquished... especially when paying to have it printed on a sign.<br/> <br/>"Think Positively" is correct.    "Positive" is a noun.   "Positively" is an adverb... it describes HOW one thinks...  Or SHOULD think, I think, says the sign.  :)<br/> <br/>*sigh*  Yes... I know that''s not your fault.   Not counting off for their bad grammar.  *grin*</td>', 'Gee.   Good grammar should not be relinquished... especially when paying to have it printed on a sign. "Think Positively" is correct.    "Positive" is a noun.   "Positively" is an adverb... it describes HOW one thinks...  Or SHOULD think, I think, says the sign.  :) *sigh*  Yes... I know that''s not your fault.   Not counting off for their bad grammar.  *grin*', '2009-04-25 22:07:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5452173, 784447, 86447, '<td valign="top">I''m sure you''ve heard that you''ve missed the spelling here...  So I won''t mention it.  :)</td>', 'I''m sure you''ve heard that you''ve missed the spelling here...  So I won''t mention it.  :)', '2009-04-25 22:11:21.000000', NULL, 1),
