(5457789, 783604, 83181, '<td valign="top">Thanks for some nice critique, I learned some again :) I''m sorry to say that, i really don''t understand many of the pics scorring higher than this in the challenge ( not all, some where very nice ) I mean, a standard picture of a streetsign saying something funny? Are you serious ? And in general I don''t see why a picture of someone elses artwork can even enter the challenges, without naming the artist creating the sculptures starring in the pictures. come on people! taking a poor picture of someone elses bad joke shouldn''t take me anywhere near the top! <br/> <br/>I appreciate all comments. Keep em coming!<br/></td>', 'Thanks for some nice critique, I learned some again :) I''m sorry to say that, i really don''t understand many of the pics scorring higher than this in the challenge ( not all, some where very nice ) I mean, a standard picture of a streetsign saying something funny? Are you serious ? And in general I don''t see why a picture of someone elses artwork can even enter the challenges, without naming the artist creating the sculptures starring in the pictures. come on people! taking a poor picture of someone elses bad joke shouldn''t take me anywhere near the top!  I appreciate all comments. Keep em coming!', '2009-04-29 16:44:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5457921, 784409, 39057, '<td valign="top">Nice setup !</td>', 'Nice setup !', '2009-04-29 18:41:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5457939, 784283, 61961, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote in the challenge, but since you asked for comments... I think she is lovely and your concept was a clever reponse to the theme.  I''m not crazy about her "extreme diagonal" position in the frame, but that''s just me. :-)  Concept-wise, I wonder if you''d make a stronger statement with more glamour to contrast with the casts.  The idea is there but it doesn''t jump out at you; perhaps it would with a bit more emphasis on dress and jewelry (or perhaps the garden setting isn''t glam enough?).  Anyhow, despite these criticisms I like the photo.</td>', 'I didn''t vote in the challenge, but since you asked for comments... I think she is lovely and your concept was a clever reponse to the theme.  I''m not crazy about her "extreme diagonal" position in the frame, but that''s just me. :-)  Concept-wise, I wonder if you''d make a stronger statement with more glamour to contrast with the casts.  The idea is there but it doesn''t jump out at you; perhaps it would with a bit more emphasis on dress and jewelry (or perhaps the garden setting isn''t glam enough?).  Anyhow, despite these criticisms I like the photo.', '2009-04-29 18:56:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5457949, 784366, 53964, '<td valign="top">Why is this "creepy"?  Thank you for entering this, and making me really think about our reactions and attitudes toward those who are different, in whatever way. I''ve learned a little about myself because of it.</td>', 'Why is this "creepy"?  Thank you for entering this, and making me really think about our reactions and attitudes toward those who are different, in whatever way. I''ve learned a little about myself because of it.', '2009-04-29 19:04:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(5457960, 784366, 105167, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jotaga:</b></div><hr/><i> The exposure is OK, but i think the composition could be improved, framing the entire notebook screen, and using the digonals of the sides of the notebook too... Besides, the title has a bad taste for me... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the comment.  I''m not quite sure what you mean "framing the entire notebook screen, and using the diagonals of the sides of the notebook too", please explain.<br/> <br/>Also, how exactly does that title offend you?</td>', 'Originally posted by jotaga: The exposure is OK, but i think the composition could be improved, framing the entire notebook screen, and using the digonals of the sides of the notebook too... Besides, the title has a bad taste for me...   Thanks for the comment.  I''m not quite sure what you mean "framing the entire notebook screen, and using the diagonals of the sides of the notebook too", please explain. Also, how exactly does that title offend you?', '2009-04-29 19:23:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5457985, 784366, 105167, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kenskid:</b></div><hr/><i> LoL...don''t mean to laugh..but on DPC you never know...is that your real hand !?!?!? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes, I''ve had it my entire life. <i>lol</i></td>', 'Originally posted by kenskid: LoL...don''t mean to laugh..but on DPC you never know...is that your real hand !?!?!?   Yes, I''ve had it my entire life. lol', '2009-04-29 19:37:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5458015, 784366, 105167, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Teafran:</b></div><hr/><i> Most likely the winner of the challenge, this is just excellant and perfectly matches the challenge subject not to mention that the image is very nicely composed. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the nice words.  This is the highest I''ve ranked so far out of 3 challenges, I didn''t know what to expect as a response to this photo.<br/> <br/>Ah...if only the others voters thought like you...oh well, on to the next challenge.</td>', 'Originally posted by Teafran: Most likely the winner of the challenge, this is just excellant and perfectly matches the challenge subject not to mention that the image is very nicely composed.   Thanks for the nice words.  This is the highest I''ve ranked so far out of 3 challenges, I didn''t know what to expect as a response to this photo. Ah...if only the others voters thought like you...oh well, on to the next challenge.', '2009-04-29 19:50:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5458019, 784283, 45475, '<td valign="top">I connected with the shot because of personal experience. So for me, the concept of ''happy, pretty young girl with ugly injury/disability = not quite right'' came through loud and clear, and I voted highly.<br/> <br/>One thing that did occur to me however, was the method of b&amp;w conversion. Her complexion looks too waxy and lip definition is almost non-existent (which is an important consideration because her smile plays a big role here). Using the red filter (and max white) when converting to b&amp;w will typically cause this to happen.<br/> <br/>The low score could just be a simple matter of folk not liking the edit. These days, with people complaining about comments and angry pm''s, not many will risk telling you they don''t like your artistic choices...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-04-29 19:01:00.</i></td>', 'I connected with the shot because of personal experience. So for me, the concept of ''happy, pretty young girl with ugly injury/disability = not quite right'' came through loud and clear, and I voted highly. One thing that did occur to me however, was the method of b&w conversion. Her complexion looks too waxy and lip definition is almost non-existent (which is an important consideration because her smile plays a big role here). Using the red filter (and max white) when converting to b&w will typically cause this to happen. The low score could just be a simple matter of folk not liking the edit. These days, with people complaining about comments and angry pm''s, not many will risk telling you they don''t like your artistic choices...', '2009-04-29 20:00:19.000000', '2009-04-29 20:01:00.000000', 0),
(5458027, 784366, 105167, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BeeCee:</b></div><hr/><i> Why is this "creepy"?  Thank you for entering this, and making me really think about our reactions and attitudes toward those who are different, in whatever way. I''ve learned a little about myself because of it. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yea, "creepy" was a little unexpected, but we put our work up here to be critiqued right, so I guess anything goes.  I''m good with it, and I also kind of expected mixed reactions to it anyway.<br/> <br/>I''m glad I could help, although unintentionally, I''m glad.  Thank you for the comments.<br/> <br/>BTW, from the looks of your portfolio, you seem to have gotten the hang of that D40 pretty well.<br/>Keep shooting, and posting!</td>', 'Originally posted by BeeCee: Why is this "creepy"?  Thank you for entering this, and making me really think about our reactions and attitudes toward those who are different, in whatever way. I''ve learned a little about myself because of it.   Yea, "creepy" was a little unexpected, but we put our work up here to be critiqued right, so I guess anything goes.  I''m good with it, and I also kind of expected mixed reactions to it anyway. I''m glad I could help, although unintentionally, I''m glad.  Thank you for the comments. BTW, from the looks of your portfolio, you seem to have gotten the hang of that D40 pretty well.Keep shooting, and posting!', '2009-04-29 20:07:59.000000', NULL, 0),
