(5460647, 783767, 59029, '<td valign="top">I don''t have time to verify this beastie''s identity right now, but at a guess I''d say it''s a Lippman, that style is quite primitive and yes, indigenous to the States.  Nice job of selective desat btw!<br/> <br/>Actually according to my sources, it''s probably an Armitage Herschell (1885), or a copy of one :-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-05-03 18:00:02.</i></td>', 'I don''t have time to verify this beastie''s identity right now, but at a guess I''d say it''s a Lippman, that style is quite primitive and yes, indigenous to the States.  Nice job of selective desat btw! Actually according to my sources, it''s probably an Armitage Herschell (1885), or a copy of one :-)', '2009-05-01 08:32:15.000000', '2009-05-03 19:00:02.000000', 0),
